summary: |
  Nine rounds on a two-document diff. 72 candidates, 35 verified and fixed, 37
  refuted on evidence. Gate 0 green at every round; no design artifact in scope,
  so five dimensions throughout and no design section here.

  Where the defects were. Not one verified finding across nine rounds touched the
  raw per-role appendix, and round 6 confirmed commit by commit that it was never
  edited. Eight were derived-layer arithmetic - a find/verify ratio range, three
  pooled medians, a misapplied superlative, three phase-path cells - and all eight
  are mechanically checkable against the appendix, which is why follow-up 7 hands
  W3 that check and the test/v2 note records it as a fifth reproducibility check
  the plan never asked for. The rest were narrative: two label counts needing
  external cr notes, one causal misattribution, a dead anchor and unrendered
  mermaid labels, prose disagreeing with an adjacent table, and prose disagreeing
  with the tip's own notes.

  That last class is the run's own finding about itself. It was the headline
  defect in four consecutive rounds - a count or taxonomy restated in a git note
  and left to drift from the document. Round 7 stopped patching it and removed the
  source: the review tally now lives only in the result's evidence table and the
  defect taxonomy only in follow-up 7, with both notes pointing rather than
  copying. Rounds 8 and 9 found none of that class.

  Two instrument failures stand in the artifact, both declared: role self-timing
  is unusable, and five phase-table cells are lower bounds whose true values died
  with the session log. Two shortfalls stand too - the design probe never ran, so
  the epic's section 3b requirement is wholly unmet, and the complex band's verify
  is n=2 and cannot be completed because the candidate text did not survive. All
  four are recorded as such and owned by follow-ups 1, 8 and 9's deviations rather
  than re-scoped away.

  The verdict is PASS on the caller's instruction to close at round 9, not on a
  clean sweep: two waivers above name what that costs. Rounds 8 and 9 each found
  exactly one defect where earlier rounds found seven and eight, and both were in
  the report's account of itself rather than in its measurements - but the trend
  is four data points, and this WU has already had two findings refuted for
  asserting trends from counts this small, so no convergence claim is made here.
